### Summary
This paper proposes a two-stage framework combining Whisper-Large-v3 ASR with an LLM (LLaMA) using LoRA-based fine-tuning for second-pass rescoring of N-best hypotheses, specifically targeting medication name recognition errors in low-resource healthcare settings. The authors curate a custom dataset called Pharma-Speak containing approximately 600 medication names and demonstrate improvements over fine-tuning the ASR model alone. The work addresses a practically important problem: ASR errors on medication names can jeopardize patient safety.

### Strengths
